<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Byzantine Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Byzantines, Byzantium, Eastern Empire, Byzantine</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Byzantine Empire was the continuation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a> in the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>, ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> from the fourth century until the city fell to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> in 1453. Greek in language and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> Christian in religion, it preserved <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-law">Roman law</a> and classical learning. It was a long-standing rival or neighbour of the Sasanian, Umayyad, Abbasid, Seljuk and Ottoman empires and an ally of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khazar-khaganate">Khazar Khaganate</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire.jpg" alt="Byzantine Empire" width="320" height="196" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mnohohrishnyi · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eastern_Roman_Empire_565_CE.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
